            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "- **Perseverance has now driven a “marathon” on Mars.** NASA reports the rover surpassed **26.2 miles (42.195 km)** of total driving on **sol 1,890**, and an **orbital HiRISE image from June 13, 2026** shows Perseverance as a small speck with its winding track line across terrain west of Jezero Crater (in an area the team calls “Arbot”).【5:0†source】\n\n- **Perseverance recently imaged Earth disappearing behind Mars’ moon Phobos.** A NASA Mars “News & Features” item dated **Aug. 5, 2026** describes a sequence/composite from Perseverance’s **Mastcam‑Z** showing **Earth as a bright dot** moving and then being **occulted by Phobos** in the Martian sky.【5:1†source】【5:3†source】\n\n- **Earlier in 2026, Perseverance completed the first AI-planned drives on another planet.** NASA/JPL says the rover executed drives on **Dec. 8 and 10, 2025** using **generative AI (vision-language models)** to select route waypoints—work led at JPL and done in collaboration with **Anthropic (Claude models)**—demonstrating more autonomous operations for future missions.【5:4†source】\n\nIf you tell me whether you want “latest” as *NASA-only updates* or *any outlet reporting about Perseverance*, I can summarize accordingly (e.g., mission status vs. science discoveries vs. tech milestones).",
